# DBTITLE 1,A3 Table Types Header
# MAGIC %md
# MAGIC ## A.3 — Table and View Types in Databricks
# MAGIC
# MAGIC Databricks supports several storage objects. Understanding **when to use each** is critical:
# MAGIC
# MAGIC | Type | Persisted? | Auto-refresh? | Best for |
# MAGIC |------|-----------|--------------|----------|
# MAGIC | **Managed Table** | ✅ Data + metadata in UC | No | Bronze/Silver/Gold layers, ETL output |
# MAGIC | **External Table** | ✅ Data in your storage | No | Data shared across platforms |
# MAGIC | **View** | ❌ Logical only | N/A (computed on read) | Reusable query logic, row-level security |
# MAGIC | **Materialized View** | ✅ Pre-computed results | ✅ In Lakeflow pipelines | Gold aggregations, dashboard acceleration |
# MAGIC | **Streaming Table** | ✅ Append-only | ✅ In Lakeflow pipelines | Real-time/incremental ingestion |
# MAGIC
# MAGIC > **💡 Tip:** In the Preferred Supplier List pipeline, we use **managed tables** for Bronze/Silver/Gold
# MAGIC > layers (simple, governed, performant). In Section D, we'll convert this to a **Lakeflow pipeline**
# MAGIC > using streaming tables and materialized views.

