# DBTITLE 1,D3 Expectations summary
# MAGIC %md
# MAGIC ## D.3 — Data Quality with Lakeflow Expectations
# MAGIC
# MAGIC Expectations are the built-in data validation feature of Lakeflow pipelines:
# MAGIC
# MAGIC | Mode | Behavior | Use when |
# MAGIC |------|---------|----------|
# MAGIC | `EXPECT (condition)` | **Warn** — log violation, keep the row | Non-critical checks (e.g., optional fields) |
# MAGIC | `EXPECT ... ON VIOLATION DROP ROW` | **Quarantine** — drop failing rows | Data quality filters (e.g., NULL keys) |
# MAGIC | `EXPECT ... ON VIOLATION FAIL UPDATE` | **Fail** — stop the entire pipeline | Critical invariants (e.g., unknown BU code) |
# MAGIC
# MAGIC ### Monitoring Expectations
# MAGIC The Lakeflow pipeline UI shows:
# MAGIC * **Pass/fail counts** per expectation per run
# MAGIC * **Trend over time** — are quality issues increasing?
# MAGIC * **Which rows were dropped** (in the event log)
# MAGIC
# MAGIC > **💡 Enbridge-specific example:** We set `known_business_unit` as `FAIL UPDATE` because
# MAGIC > an unknown BU code means the data source changed and needs human review.

